<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- 513, the Tyrant room. The entry scene breaks the pod and the Tyrant
     (id 0x0C) wakes; the <fight> holds the room until it is dead (enemy
     bit 112). The init takes one of two branches on common bit 5B:

     Clear (Wesker's branch): the Tyrant kills Wesker; the master key (AOT 2,
     item bit 0x5F) is an item zone from the start, but its model shows, and
     the room's main lets it be taken, only once the Tyrant is dead. The
     death also sets room bit 3 and scenario 0x37, turns door 0 (to 514)
     into message 159 and AOT 1 into the room's control device: Yes unlocks
     the door (SCE_DOOR again) and sets room bit 6. Room bit 3 is set only
     on the entry the Tyrant dies in; on a later one scenario 0x37 leaves
     door 0 a door and AOT 1 a plain message.

     Set (Barry's branch): door 0 is message 131 and AOT 1 message 160
     for the whole entry. The death turns AOT 3 at (4166, 6696) into
     event_17 (Barry's scene), whose end makes door 0 a door again and sets
     no flag. So its step is done while common 5B is clear (the other
     branch) or once door 0 is a live door (`opens`), and the control
     device's step is done once door 0 is a door too (the death sets room
     bit 3 in this branch as well). -->
<bot format="2">
  <fight enemy="0x0C" bank="3" bit="112" label="the Tyrant"/>
  <interact slot="3" bank="1" bit="0x5B" done="clear" opens="0"
            label="Barry's event: door 0 opens"/>
  <interact slot="1" bank="4" bit="6" after_bank="4" after_bit="3" opens="0"
            label="the control device: unlock door 0"/>
  <answer choice="yes" slot="1"/>
</bot>
